cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline: Tumor-naive cfDNA Cancer Detection via 5Mb + 100kb Short/Long Ratio, Median-Normalized Coverage, and FSD Histogram"
authors:
  - given-names: "Yu Ching"
    family-names: "Lam"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher (no institutional affiliation; verified email domain umich.edu)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9113-769X"
year: 2026
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.to-be-assigned-on-first-release"
url: "https://github.com/rollroyces/cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rollroyces/cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline"
repository-companion: "https://github.com/rollroyces/deepcatch"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: 2026-08-23
keywords:
  - "cfDNA"
  - "ctDNA"
  - "fragmentomics"
  - "DELFI"
  - "cross-study"
  - "harmonization"
  - "pan-cancer"
  - "open science"
abstract: >
  cfdna-fragmentomics-pipeline is an open-source tumor-naive cfDNA
  cancer detection pipeline that runs on FinaleDB pre-computed fragment
  records. The pipeline extracts a 5-channel profile (5Mb + 100kb
  short/long ratio, 5Mb + 100kb median-normalized coverage, and the
  full 196-bin fragment-size distribution) per sample, then trains an
  LR-on-PCA classifier with optional per-study z-score harmonization.
  On a cross-study pan-cancer cohort of 627 FinaleDB samples (363
  cancer + 264 healthy from Jiang 2015 + Cristiano 2019), the pipeline
  achieves AUC 0.9745 +/- 0.002 (5-seed, harmonized), at parity with
  DELFI-HCC on the clinically relevant Sens@95% metric. The pipeline
  is intentionally a separate package — consumed by DeepCatch via a
  thin adapter that reads only the .npy/JSON file format. All code
  (MIT), data (open access), and results are freely available.
references:
